# The root .gitignore ignores `out/` for Next.js. A bare pattern like that matches at *every* level,
# so it also swallows contracts/out — which is exactly what this lane publishes for the other four
# (master plan §10 Lane A). A .gitignore in a deeper directory overrides a shallower one, so
# re-include it here rather than editing shared root config that Wave 0 owns.
!/out/

# `build_info = false` in foundry.toml keeps these out of a normal build, but `forge inspect`
# regenerates them regardless. They are solc input/output JSON that no downstream lane reads — the
# ABIs and bytecode are in the per-contract artifacts — so keep them out of the committed tree.
/out/build-info/

# Artifacts for the *test* tree. Nothing outside this lane integrates against a test contract's ABI,
# and committing them cost more than they were worth twice over: they are the bulk of the diff noise
# every lane sees on a `contracts/` commit, and their solc metadata carries dozens of IPFS CIDs that
# a credential scanner reasonably reads as high-entropy secrets. The artifacts for `src/` — the ones
# the convention above exists for — are still committed and still published.
/out/*.t.sol/
/out/VaultTestBase.sol/
/out/VaultHandler.sol/

# Foundry local state. Already covered by the root file; repeated so this directory is
# self-explanatory to anyone who opens it alone.
/cache/
/broadcast/
